er-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-4x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=4x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/1c701d81ab131757758e19c3c1d9813f1e8cda3ff069843c9105dd125d1caf97.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ba6ec0ff0bd36366ee3365452b59a030a352a8435f5099b4a23a938cf89a68c"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4x"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}x"] ["math" "4x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json" "file_sha256" "150f600fed24a0b162119b5e3580d586627bf74d4449048d83c83c5ac600b48a"} {"question" "q-332643" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x"] ["math" "-x"] ["math" "2x"] ["math" "x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/state.json